# K09-L quad tailsitter - ArduPilot Plane parameter file (owner F4, revision F4-R11, 2026-11-14, D-174: limiter 80 A, gate 2.70 kg,
#   Gens Ace LiHV 4S 6000 HV Shorty (17.4 V full): THR_MAX 41, FWD_BAT / Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX 17.4, BATT_* for the pack. R10 D-173: SunnySky
#   X2814 V3 KV900 + APC 11x8E/EP, Q_M_SPIN_MAX 0.81 fixed, limiter 75 A; D-173b: back to the CoreWing F405 Wing V2, the Lua spin
#   cap of R9 (D-161c) is WITHDRAWN: no SCR_* lines (the CoreWing build has no scripting, so they would be unknown names; the
#   script is archived in subsystems/flight-software/archive/D-161c/). R9: CR-F5-15/16, BATT_LOW 3 000; R8: CR-C1-40, B3 entry
#   design; R7 design round D-145..D-157; R6 CDR fix round D-120..D-126)
# Status: PROPOSED. Not loaded on hardware. Loaded and read back in SITL (ArduPlane 4.7.3-beta1 Windows build,
#   2026-11-13, team/F4/sitl/RESULTS.md): every name below is accepted except SERVO_BLH_BDMASK / SERVO_BLH_POLES,
#   which the SITL build does not carry (board only: T-F3-FW-LOAD). Flight behaviour on K09-L: UNVERIFIED.
# Firmware: ArduPlane 4.7.2 stable or later, target CoreWingF405WingV2 (D-33, D-173b; the board entered ArduPilot in 4.7.2,
#   ReleaseNotes "Changes from 4.7.1", read 2026-11-13; bdshot on outputs 1-4, no Lua on this board).
# Parameter names: every name is in ArduPilot's published Plane parameter definitions for stable-4.7.1
#   (https://autotest.ardupilot.org/Parameters/versioned/Plane/stable-4.7.1/apm.pdef.xml, read 2026-11-13; the 4.7.2
#   folder is not published). fsw_check.py checks every name against team/F4/ap_plane_param_names_4.7.1.txt offline.
# R6 name changes (4.7): FS_SHORT_TIMEOUT removed by the firmware -> RC_FS_TIMEOUT; Q_A_ACCEL_Y_MAX (cdeg/s/s) is
#   Q_A_ACC_Y_MAX (deg/s/s); the six LEGACY duplicates (Q_WP_SPEED_DN, Q_PILOT_SPEED_DN, Q_LAND_SPEED, GPS_POS1_X/Y/Z)
#   are deleted: no firmware that knows them runs on this board.
# Format: one comment line (or more) above every parameter, then NAME,VALUE. "(default, stated)" marks a line that
#   repeats the firmware default on purpose because a request names it.
# Frame: params.json#frame (x aft, y right, z up, cruise attitude). Hover copter frame: forward = belly (-z),
#   right = right wing (+y), down = tail (+x). Motor map: SPEC.md. Bench/stand set: K09L-STAND.param (load after).
# Re-check: python -I redesign/team/F4/fsw_check.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1 Frame: copter-motor tailsitter
# enable the QuadPlane VTOL code (reboot after setting)
Q_ENABLE,1
# tailsitter: hover nose-up on the same four motors; 1 = enabled with Q_ modes (2 = always, not used)
Q_TAILSIT_ENABLE,1
# copter frame class Quad (default, stated: R-FSW-PARAMS)
Q_FRAME_CLASS,1
# copter frame type X (default, stated). Not 17 NYT_X: elevons have no hover authority (CR-B4-06e); hover yaw is prop torque + 7 deg cant
Q_FRAME_TYPE,1
# all four motors stay active in fixed-wing flight (bitmask motors 1-4): they are the cruise propulsion
Q_TAILSIT_MOTMX,15
# 262400 = bit 18 ARMVTOL (arm only in a Q mode, J1 failure mode 8) + bit 8 Mtrs_Only_Qassist (assist uses motors, elevons stay plane-controlled). Bit 5 off: RC loss in a Q mode -> QLAND
Q_OPTIONS,262400
# start in QSTABILIZE, never MANUAL (default MANUAL would pass raw sticks to a hovering tailsitter); R-SPIRAL (D-66) also
#   bars it: CL-F4-NO-RAW-MODES counts INITIAL_MODE with FLTMODE1-6
INITIAL_MODE,17

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2 Outputs (F3 CR-F3-02: outputs 1-4 bdshot on TIM4/TIM3, elevons 5-6 on TIM8 PWM, 7 unused)
# out 1 = Motor 1 = station LR (lower right), CCW seen from the nose, APC 11x8E (D-173), right-hand-thread adapter
SERVO1_FUNCTION,33
# out 2 = Motor 2 = station UL (upper left), CCW seen from the nose, APC 11x8E, right-hand-thread adapter
SERVO2_FUNCTION,34
# out 3 = Motor 3 = station LL (lower left), CW seen from the nose, APC 11x8EP, LEFT-hand-thread adapter (CR-E1-21: prop drag tightens the nut)
SERVO3_FUNCTION,35
# out 4 = Motor 4 = station UR (upper right), CW seen from the nose, APC 11x8EP, LEFT-hand-thread adapter (CR-E1-21)
SERVO4_FUNCTION,36
# out 5 = left elevon servo (ElevonLeft); throw limits in section 2b
SERVO5_FUNCTION,77
# out 6 = right elevon servo (ElevonRight)
SERVO6_FUNCTION,78
# motor outputs DShot300 (Bluejay reflash of the LANRC BLHeli_S ESC, E1)
Q_M_PWM_TYPE,5
# bidirectional DShot on outputs 1-4 for ESC rpm telemetry (harmonic notch, rpm cap check)
SERVO_BLH_BDMASK,15
# motor magnet poles for rpm = eRPM / (poles/2); SunnySky X2814 V3 (D-173): pole count — (UNVERIFIED: count the magnets, CR-F4-06)
SERVO_BLH_POLES,14
# ESC type for DShot commands: 1 = BLHeli32/BLHeli_S/Kiss family (UNVERIFIED for Bluejay; bench check)
SERVO_DSHOT_ESC,1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2b Elevon throw (D6 CR-D6-09; CALC-F4-ELEVON-PWM)
# Starting values from D6's linkage: the servo turns +44.7 deg for TE up 25 deg and -42.9 deg for TE down 25 deg
#   (CL-D6-THROW-NEED, CALC-D6-KIN), at 500 us per 45 deg (ASM-D6-SERVO-THROW, 11.1 us/deg). Each side gets its own
#   MIN and MAX so a full demand gives exactly +/-25 deg at the trailing edge. FINAL VALUES COME FROM T-D6-THROW
#   (protractor on the TE, both sides): replace these lines, never exceed 1000-2000 us without D6.
#   Sense assumed: right servo, higher pulse = TE up; left servo mirrored, so REVERSED 1. If the bench shows the
#   right TE going down on a higher pulse, set both REVERSED the other way and swap the up/down offsets below.
# left: reversed (mirror of the right servo, CR-D6-09)
SERVO5_REVERSED,1
# left neutral 1500 us (trim set on the bench with the panel on the airfoil line)
SERVO5_TRIM,1500
# left TE-up end: reversed, so the low end; 1500 - 44.7 x 11.1 = 1003 us
SERVO5_MIN,1003
# left TE-down end: 1500 + 42.9 x 11.1 = 1976 us
SERVO5_MAX,1976
# right: normal sense
SERVO6_REVERSED,0
# right neutral 1500 us
SERVO6_TRIM,1500
# right TE-down end: 1500 - 42.9 x 11.1 = 1024 us
SERVO6_MIN,1024
# right TE-up end: 1500 + 44.7 x 11.1 = 1997 us
SERVO6_MAX,1997
# elevon mixer gain 0.65 (was 0.5, the default; CDR-14, board decision B9, D-120): pure pitch or pure roll reaches
#   0.65 x 25 = 16.25 deg; both together saturate at 25 deg, so full pitch leaves 8.75 deg of roll. The pure-pitch travel
#   sets B3's forward CG limit (CL-B3-V-CG-FWD reads P:fsw.mixing_gain); the trimmed CLmax needs 11.0 deg at the CG
#   target (CL-B3-DELTA-STALL), inside 16.25 (CL-F4-MIX-PITCH). Documented range 0.5-1.2 (pdef 4.7.1)
MIXING_GAIN,0.65

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3 Motor limits (E1, B4, C1, A2)
# output at full demand 0.81, FIXED (F4-R10, A1 D-173, E1 "D-173 motor"): one motor at full output with the others light on a
#   fresh pack (the worst case for current) stays at 49.3 A winding <= 50 A / 30 s (X2814 V3) and 40.0 A ESC <= 45 A; on the
#   worst-state pack the 75 A limiter binds before 0.81, so worst T/W 1.762 (band edge) is unchanged. Was 0.746 + Lua schedule
#   (R9, withdrawn D-173b). Range 0.9-1.0 is metadata only (SITL S1 keeps 0.84 / 0.746 / 0.81)
Q_M_SPIN_MAX,0.81
# pack-current limiter 80 A (F4-R11, A1 D-174: P:performance.full_throttle_current_a 80.0, gate 2.70 kg; D-173 had 75, D-161
#   73.2, D-157 70.2, D-148 70, was 100). E1 D-173 limiter table: at 80 A, 2.64 kg fresh T/W 2.102, worst 1.826, winding 29.1 A
#   (<= 50), ESC 20.0 A; largest mass with B3's 1.75 is 2.755 kg. Claim CL-F4-BAT-CURR-MAX. Valid only with the current sensor
#   within +/-1.1 % at 70-80 A: T-F1-SENSOR-CAL must pass and BATT_AMP_PERVLT carry its value BEFORE FLIGHT. AP_Float, 0-200 A
Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX,80
# limiter reads battery monitor 0 = the flight pack (default, stated: CR-A2-14)
Q_M_BAT_IDX,0
# limiter time constant 1 s (default 5 s): C1 shows a step to full throttle outruns a slow limiter (CL-C1-T-CAP)
Q_M_BAT_CURR_TC,1
# built-in VTOL voltage compensation, LiHV 4S full 4 x 4.35 = 17.4 V (F4-R11, D-174 Gens Ace HV Shorty; R10 16.8 for LiPo).
#   The firmware clamps the resting voltage to [MIN, MAX] and scales demand by MAX / V, so MAX must be the full-charge voltage:
#   a fresh LiHV pack then reads ratio 1 (AP_Motors_Thrust_Linearization.cpp, tag Plane-4.7.2). Full demand still maps to 0.81
Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX,17.4
# 3.30 V/cell
Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN,13.2
# lowest running output 0.15 (default, stated: CALC-F4-VLEVEL input); the stand sets the value that spins reliably (TUNING-PLAN step 2)
Q_M_SPIN_MIN,0.15
# thrust-curve expo 0.65 (default, stated: CALC-F4-VLEVEL input); replace from the stand thrust-vs-output curve
Q_M_THST_EXPO,0.65
# hover throttle start value 0.49 (E1, X3108S; the X2814 V3 + 11x8E hover value is learnt on the first hover: about 0.45 EST
#   from E1's 5 693 rpm); learnt in flight (Q_M_HOVER_LEARN 2 below). The forward-transition entry is a
#   ratio to the learnt value (1.285 x theta_h, section 5), so this start value does not set it
Q_M_THST_HOVER,0.49
# hover-throttle learning on, learnt value saved (default 2, stated: B3 closure section 1.4). It does not move in QSTABILIZE
#   (update_throttle_hover returns while the Z controller is off, B3 section 1.2)
Q_M_HOVER_LEARN,2
# fixed-wing throttle ceiling 41 % on a full pack (F4-R11, D-174 LiHV; R10 42 at 16.8 V, R8 / R9 60, before 70). F4 estimate (EST;
#   APC PER3 11x8E, E1's two prop factors, X2814 V3 Kv 900 / 33.6 mOhm, B4's CD0 / k, 2.70 kg, 10 deg cant): on a fresh 17.4 V
#   pack the output that reaches VH 21.76 = VD 27.2 / 1.25 is 0.414; 0.41 -> 21.24-21.53 m/s (CL-F4-VLEVEL-VH 0.989). FW output
#   passes straight through (tailsitter.cpp output() -> output_motor_mask(), tag Plane-4.7.2: ASM-F4-FW-PASSTHRU). FWD_BAT_VOLT_*
#   raise this ceiling as the pack sags: a 14.4 V resting pack flies 19.97-20.2 m/s >= AIRSPEED_MAX 18. B4 to confirm (CR-F4-54)
THR_MAX,41
# forward-throttle battery compensation (F4-R10 / R11): demand and THR_MAX / THR_MIN scale by FWD_BAT_VOLT_MAX / resting V
#   (servos.cpp FWD_BATT_CMP, tag Plane-4.7.2), so the terminal voltage at THR_MAX stays 0.41 x 17.4 = 7.13 V on any pack
#   (<= 0.414 x 17.4 = 7.21 V for VH). LiHV 4S full 17.4 V (D-174). THR_MAX <= 100 x MIN / MAX = 75 holds (41 x 17.4 / 13.2 = 54 %)
FWD_BAT_VOLT_MAX,17.4
# compensation floor 3.30 V/cell (below this no further scaling)
FWD_BAT_VOLT_MIN,13.2
# compensation reads battery monitor 0 = the flight pack (default, stated)
FWD_BAT_IDX,0
# fixed-wing throttle floor 10 %: keeps differential-thrust yaw damping when TECS idles (CR-B3-15: optional damping)
THR_MIN,10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 4 Hover (Q modes)
# hover lean limit 30 deg (default, stated): 5 m/s lean 16 deg (P:performance.lean_5ms_deg), tip-over 30 deg
Q_A_ANGLE_MAX,30
# hover body-rate limits (deg/s): <= 3 rad/s = 172 deg/s assumed by C1 (CR-C1-08)
Q_A_RATE_R_MAX,120
# copter pitch = upper vs lower pair
Q_A_RATE_P_MAX,120
# copter yaw = rotation about the aircraft x axis; slowest axis (prop torque + 7 deg cant)
Q_A_RATE_Y_MAX,90
# starting rate gains (PROPOSED). Crossover ceilings hold until T-C2-TAP-TEST gives the symmetric torsion mode and a static
#   notch is set on it (CR-B3-19): pitch <= 4.5 Hz, yaw <= 2.4 Hz, roll held to 4.5 Hz too (tighter than CR-C2-03's 5).
#   Copter roll (L/R pairs, arm 0.32 m, Izz from A3) 1.1 Hz at these gains (CL-F4-XOVER-RLL); P ceiling 0.34
Q_A_RAT_RLL_P,0.08
Q_A_RAT_RLL_I,0.08
Q_A_RAT_RLL_D,0.002
# D-term filter 32 Hz (default 20): >= 2 x the 14.9 Hz top of the wing torsion band (CL-F4-FILT-SEP)
Q_A_RAT_RLL_FLTD,32
# copter pitch = upper/lower pairs, arm 0.19 m, the stiffest axis, 2.6 Hz at these gains (CL-F4-XOVER-PIT, ceiling 4.5 Hz); P ceiling 0.14 with D 0.002
Q_A_RAT_PIT_P,0.08
Q_A_RAT_PIT_I,0.08
Q_A_RAT_PIT_D,0.002
# D-term filter 32 Hz, as roll
Q_A_RAT_PIT_FLTD,32
# copter yaw: prop torque + 7 deg cant (sense corrected, D-52: cant_sense_UR -1), 1.0 Hz at these gains (CL-F4-XOVER-YAW, ceiling 2.4 Hz: P+I only, no D, CR-B3-19); P ceiling 0.94
Q_A_RAT_YAW_P,0.40
Q_A_RAT_YAW_I,0.04
# yaw acceleration limit of the attitude shaper 135 deg/s/s = 2.36 rad/s2 (new line, CDR-16 / CDR-AE-12, D-123): 84 %
#   of what the airframe has at 30 % differential (CL-B3-HOVER-YAW-ACCEL-LOW); claim CL-F4-YAW-ACC-SET. The board asked
#   "Q_A_ACCEL_Y_MAX 13 500 cdeg/s/s": that is the 4.6 name and unit. In 4.7 the name is Q_A_ACC_Y_MAX in deg/s/s, range
#   0-720 (ReleaseNotes 4.7.0 "ATC_ACC_R/P/Y_MAX renamed and scaled to deg/s/s", PR 32192; pdef 4.7.1). 13 500 typed
#   into the 4.7 name would be out of range. Roll and pitch limits stay at the firmware default. T-B4-YAW re-sets it
Q_A_ACC_Y_MAX,135
# auto/QRTL descent 1.2 m/s: vortex-ring onset 1.88 m/s (CL-B4-DESCENT); B4 asks <= 1.5 (CR-B4-06b). Units m/s
Q_WP_SPD_DN,1.2
# pilot descent at full down stick in QHOVER/QLOITER 1.0 m/s (R5, was 1.2; default 0 = the 2.5 m/s climb limit, above
#   VRS onset). D-65: a touchdown at this rate is the design hard landing, 1.2 m/s at <= 10 deg any direction
#   (P:requirements.landing_sink_ms); 1.0 leaves 0.2 m/s for velocity-loop overshoot, no rangefinder and ground effect
#   (CL-F4-TOUCHDOWN-SINK). QSTABILIZE has no climb-rate loop (throttle is direct): never land in it (CR-F4-21)
Q_PILOT_SPD_DN,1.0
# final landing descent 0.3 m/s (was 0.5, the default; CR-D5-21, D-65): below 0.32 m/s the pre-crushed foot cartridges take a touchdown
#   elastically (CL-D5-V-NO-SET), at 0.5 they set 1.28 mm per landing (2.3 landings to the 3 mm mark). Costs ~8 s from
#   Q_LAND_FINAL_ALT. VRS onset 1.88 m/s is far away. The velocity controller holds thrust to contact (CL-F4-LAND-SPD)
Q_LAND_FINAL_SPD,0.3
# QLAND/RTL switches to the final descent speed below 6 m (default, stated: CR-D5-21 keeps it)
#   PENDING (C-07, G-06; CR-132423 p. 59): after test M1 (baro height error at touchdown, 10 flights) set this to 6 + the measured error,
#   only if |error| > 1 m (EST); the final 0.3 m/s must start above the ground. Value: — until M1. Do not change before M1
Q_LAND_FINAL_ALT,6
# PENDING (C-06, G-09; CR-132423 p. 61): Q_P_NE_VEL_P and Q_P_NE_POS_P (the 4.7 names of Q_P_VELXY_P / Q_P_POSXY_P;
#   SITL defaults 0.7 / 0.5) stay at the firmware defaults (no line here) until SITL S3b / the
#   tethered 1 m/s step in TUNING-PLAN.md measures the QLOITER velocity-loop crossover. Pass: <= 1/6 of the attitude crossover = <= 1.0 rad/s
#   at the 1.0 Hz roll loop (CL-F4-XOVER-RLL). If it fails, lower both, add the two lines here and mirror them in params.json. Values: —
# weathervane in hover: 1 = nose into wind = belly (copter nose, -z) into wind (default on Plane, stated; J1 CR-J1-05: wind
#   loads copter pitch, the strongest axis). Acts only in position-controlled Q modes (QLOITER, QLAND, QRTL, AUTO): not in
#   QSTABILIZE or QHOVER, and not while the pilot gives yaw input (quadplane.cpp get_weathervane_yaw_rate_cds, tag Plane-4.7.1)
Q_WVANE_ENABLE,1
# weathervane gain start 1 (J1, ArduPilot weathervaning page)
Q_WVANE_GAIN,1
# landing override 1 = nose into wind = BELLY into the wind (D-152, was 3 side = wingtip into wind). C5: belly to the
#   wind lull limit 5.3 m/s, 5.7 at +/-30 deg heading error; pod face (+z) to the wind 4.5 m/s, so never 2 (nose OR
#   tail) or 4 (tail = pod face). Values -1 no override, 0 off, 1 nose, 2 nose or tail, 3 side, 4 tail
#   (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/Plane-4.7.1/libraries/AC_AttitudeControl/AC_WeatherVane.cpp, read 2026-11-14). Applies in QRTL and the VTOL land descent / final (in_vtol_land_sequence)
Q_WVANE_LAND,1
# take-off override 1 = nose into wind = BELLY into the wind (D-156, review/DESIGN-ROUND-2026-11-14/A1.md; was 3 side =
#   wingtip, B3's failing hover-yaw case): same heading as landing (D-152). Acts only in AUTO VTOL take-offs
#   (is_takeoff = in_vtol_auto() && is_vtol_takeoff, quadplane.cpp tag Plane-4.7.1, read 2026-11-14)
Q_WVANE_TAKEOFF,1
# weathervane down to the ground: no minimum height, no vertical-speed or ground-speed cut-off (Plane defaults 0, stated:
#   D-152 needs the heading held through touchdown; a positive HGT_MIN or VELZ_MAX below the descent rate would stop it)
Q_WVANE_HGT_MIN,0
Q_WVANE_VELZ_MAX,0
Q_WVANE_SPD_MAX,0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 5 Transition (TRANSITION section of SPEC.md)
# Entry design (B3 closure 1.3-1.4, replaces D-149's ">= 1.4 W"; no parameter sets it): one transmitter switch (F5) overrides
#   CH3 to throttle_in = 1.285 x learnt theta_h (0.630 at 0.49), holds QSTABILIZE for a 1.0 s pre-climb (B3 closure; L06 0.9 s, FC hold 1.08-1.38 s), then sends FBWA;
#   the override releases >= 0.5 s after FBWA. FBWA / CRUISE / RTL are never reachable from a Q mode by the plain mode switch
#   (F5 latch). The firmware holds max(hover, entry throttle_in) through ANGLE_WAIT_FW, stick ignored (tailsitter.cpp
#   Tailsitter_Transition::update, tag Plane-4.7.2, read 2026-11-14); SITL S4c confirms. Static T0/W 1.29-1.39 at the band edges
# forward pitch-over rate 12 deg/s (B3 closure: 8-16 deg/s moves the entry window by <= 0.006 W); at most 15 after the cold-pack stand run confirms sag >= 0.76 and step-7 logs show peak output <= 0.7
Q_TAILSIT_RAT_FW,12
# 11667 ms: inert while Q_TAILSIT_RAT_FW is configured; if RAT_FW were ever unconfigured the firmware derives
#   RAT_FW = Q_TAILSIT_ANGLE / (MS / 2000) = 70 / 5.83 = 12.0 deg/s (tailsitter.cpp setup(), tag Plane-4.7.2), not 70 / 2.5 = 28
#   deg/s at the Quad-frame default 5000 (quadplane.cpp). B3 closure 1.4; CL-F4-TRANS-MS-RATE
Q_TRANSITION_MS,11667
# angle boost OFF. The pitch-over calls set_throttle_out(..., apply_angle_boost = true); boost would raise the held throttle as
#   1/cos(tilt) and saturate it (B3 1.2). Must be SET: the tailsitter defaults table (Q_A_ANGLE_BOOST 0) is applied only for
#   Q_FRAME_CLASS 10 (tailsitter.cpp setup(): frame_class == MOTOR_FRAME_TAILSITTER), and K09-L is class 1 (Quad), whose default
#   is 1 (AC_AttitudeControl.cpp ANGLE_BOOST default 1, tag Plane-4.7.2, read 2026-11-14). CL-F4-ANGLE-BOOST
Q_A_ANGLE_BOOST,0
# pilot-throttle expo 0.2 (default, stated): the CH3 override value is computed through throttle_curve with it (B3 1.4)
Q_THROTTLE_EXPO,0.2
# back-transition pitch-up rate 30 deg/s (default 50); SITL S5 sweeps 20/30/50 (CR-B3-15: motors hold 1.03 N*m nose-up at 8-11 m/s)
#   C1: a back-transition entered at VD 27.2 m/s reaches n 2.82 <= 3.4 at 30 (CL-C1-N-REACH-VT reads fsw.rat_vt_degs)
Q_TAILSIT_RAT_VT,30
# plane controller takes over at 70 deg nose-down from vertical = 20 deg above the horizon (CR-B4-06d); B3 closure keeps 70 (75 pushes GUST2 over 1.0)
Q_TAILSIT_ANGLE,70
# back-transition end angle 0 = use Q_TAILSIT_ANGLE 70 (default, stated: B3 closure 1.4; tailsitter.cpp get_transition_angle_vtol)
Q_TAILSIT_ANG_VT,0
# back-transition throttle 55 % (default -1 = hover throttle 49 %): keeps thrust and wash up in the flare (J1 failure mode 3)
Q_TAILSIT_THR_VT,55
# gain scaling on throttle only (default, stated): bit 2 would schedule on airspeed in the pitch-over, which B4 forbids (CR-B4-06d)
Q_TAILSIT_GSCMSK,1
# disk loading 2.6 kg / 0.245 m^2 (CR-J1-05); inert while GSCMSK bit 2 is off
Q_TAILSIT_DSKLD,10.6
# copter assist below 14 m/s (was 13; CDR-15, B6, D-122) = 1.08 x the tripped forward-CG stall 12.94 m/s (B1 2026-11-14;
#   B1's ASM-B1-TRANS assumes 1.10 Vs = 14.2: information, no change asked). ArduPilot guidance: about 3 m/s under the
#   minimum airspeed = 17 - 3 = 14 (quadplane.cpp ASSIST_SPEED, tag Plane-4.7.1, read 2026-11-14). B3's closure entry
#   reaches 70 deg at 13.0-13.9 m/s (B3 closure band). Re-set to ceil(1.1 x measured stall) after T-B2-STALL. The only assist
#   trigger kept: below 14 m/s the stall line caps the load factor at (14 / 11.90)^2 = 1.38 <= 3.4 (CL-F4-QASSIST-N)
Q_ASSIST_SPEED,14
# altitude-triggered assist OFF (F4-R8, CR-C1-40 residual; was 15 m). On this tailsitter the assist motors are the cruise
#   motors, so assist adds no lift; it puts the motors on the copter rate loop (Q_A_RATE_P_MAX 120 deg/s, not the 35 deg/s FW
#   clamp) at any airspeed (VTOL_Assist::should_assist, tailsitter.cpp output(), tag Plane-4.7.2, read 2026-11-14). K09-L
#   never flies FW below 50 m by plan. B4 withdrew its rpm reason (CR-B4-31) after D-161; the C1 load reason stands.
#   Safety review and the alternative (assist on with Q_A_RATE_P_MAX 35): F4.md section 3. Change here and fsw.assist_alt_m
Q_ASSIST_ALT,0
# angle-triggered assist OFF (F4-R8, CR-C1-40 residual; default 30). It fires only outside the FW attitude envelope + 5 deg
#   with > this error for Q_ASSIST_DELAY 0.5 s, at any airspeed; with Q_OPTIONS bit 8 the elevons stay on the plane pitch
#   controller (PTCH2SRV_RMAX clamp kept) but the motors run the copter rate loop up to 120 deg/s: the clamp is bypassed through
#   the motors. Stall upsets are covered by the speed trigger. CL-F4-QASSIST-TRIGGERS; F4.md section 3. Change here and
#   fsw.assist_angle_deg
Q_ASSIST_ANGLE,0
# transition time limit 15 s (B1 needs 7.8 s to 1.3 Vs at 12 deg/s, CL-B1-TRANS-TIME)
Q_TRANS_FAIL,15
# on transition failure: QRTL (R-FAILSAFES)
Q_TRANS_FAIL_ACT,1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 6 Fixed-wing envelope and elevon schedule (B1, B3, C1: D-29, D-36)
# cruise target 17 m/s (D-122; D-145 2026-11-14 sets P:performance.cruise_ms and transition_min_ms to 17 to match): the
#   tripped-boundary-layer stall is the planning baseline until T-B2-STALL
AIRSPEED_CRUISE,17
# TECS floor 17 m/s (was 16; B6, D-122; D-145 confirms, = P:performance.transition_min_ms 17) >= 1.3 x the tripped
#   forward-CG stall = 16.82 (CL-F4-ARSPD-TRIP-NEED; claim CL-F4-ARSPD-MIN-TRIP). Integer parameter (AP_Int16). Holds for a
#   measured stall <= 17 / 1.3 = 13.07 m/s. NOT FROZEN: after T-B2-STALL set ceil(1.3 x measured trimmed stall): <= 12.31 m/s
#   -> 16 only if A1 also moves transition_min_ms (D-145); 13.07-13.85 -> the second fallback
#   (AIRSPEED_MIN = CRUISE 18, AIRSPEED_MAX 20 < VA 20.5; B2 CL-B2R3-FB2-*; needs A1's yes on AIRSPEED_MAX 20, PROPOSED)
AIRSPEED_MIN,17
# TECS ceiling 18 m/s (CR-B1-12; D-145 confirms) <= 22 asked for ARSPD_FBW_MAX (CR-C1-08; that is this parameter's pre-4.5 name) and < VA 20.5
AIRSPEED_MAX,18
# stall speed for stall-prevention bank scaling: 13 (was 12; B6, D-122) = the tripped stall 12.85 m/s rounded up
AIRSPEED_STALL,13
# airspeed the FW gains are tuned at = cruise. Surface demand scales by 17/V: 0.83 at VA 20.5, 0.63 at VD 27.2 (floor 0.47 = 17/(2 x AIRSPEED_MAX))
SCALING_SPEED,17
# bank limit 45 deg: n = 1.41 against the +3.4 limit (P:requirements.load_factor_limit_pos)
ROLL_LIMIT_DEG,45
# pitch-up limit 20 deg
PTCH_LIM_MAX_DEG,20
# pitch-down limit 10 deg (was 15): steady dive at idle then tops out at 17.8 m/s (20.1 at B1's older L/D 7.16) <= VA 20.5, so the full-travel speed is not exceeded in a FW mode (CL-F4-VDIVE-VA; at 15 deg: 26 m/s)
PTCH_LIM_MIN_DEG,-10
# FW body-rate limits (deg/s) <= 172 deg/s (C1); roll >= 90 deg/s requirement (P:requirements.roll_rate_min_degs)
RLL2SRV_RMAX,150
# pitch rate limits up 35 / down 20 deg/s (F4-R8, CR-C1-40; were 100 / 100). ArduPilot clamps the TOTAL pitch-rate demand,
#   turn offset included (AP_PitchController.cpp, tag Plane-4.7.1, C1's SRC-C1-AP-PITCHCTL), so n <= 1 + VD k q / g:
#   35 -> 3.12 <= 3.4 (C1 ceiling 39.66), 20 -> -1.21 >= -1.5 (ceiling 24.79). A 45 deg coordinated turn at AIRSPEED_MIN 17
#   needs 23.4 deg/s (CL-F4-PTCH-RMAX-TURN). Elevons only; the VTOL controller (Q_A_RATE_P_MAX) is separate
PTCH2SRV_RMAX_UP,35
PTCH2SRV_RMAX_DN,20
# TECS climb 3 m/s (CR-B1-12; FW climb 4.7 m/s at 80 % thrust)
TECS_CLMB_MAX,3
# TECS sink 2.5 m/s = 9 deg path at 16 m/s, inside the 10 deg pitch floor (was 4)
TECS_SINK_MAX,2.5
# airspeed sensor MS4525DO on I2C 0x28 (D-33, CR-F3-02)
ARSPD_TYPE,1
# I2C bus 0 (CR-F3-02)
ARSPD_BUS,0
# pitot tube order 2 = auto-detect (CR-F3-02)
ARSPD_TUBE_ORDR,2
# use the sensor for TECS and gain scaling (default 1, stated)
ARSPD_USE,1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 7 Fixed-wing yaw by differential thrust (CR-B3-15: optional damping, Cn_beta > 0)
# rudder output -> left/right motor differential, % of full output per unit rudder (default 10); 32 % holds 1.0 N*m (CL-F4-RUDD-DT-REQ)
RUDD_DT_GAIN,35
# yaw damper on the (virtual) rudder channel; builders 0.08-0.12 (J1)
YAW2SRV_DAMP,0.1
# no sideslip feedback until the twin's yaw doublet (T-B3-YAW-DOUBLET) shows it is needed
YAW2SRV_SLIP,0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 8 IMU filtering (CR-C2-03, CR-C2-04, CR-C4-07, CR-J1-12)
# gyro sample rate 0 = 1 kHz (default, stated: CR-F3-02)
INS_GYRO_RATE,0
# gyro low-pass 40 Hz (default 20): 2.7 x the 14.9 Hz top of the antisymmetric wing torsion band; motor noise is taken by the notch
INS_GYRO_FILTER,40
# rpm-tracking harmonic notch on
INS_HNTCH_ENABLE,1
# mode 3 = ESC telemetry (bidirectional DShot)
INS_HNTCH_MODE,3
# reference 1: required for rpm/ESC tracking (0 freezes the notch at INS_HNTCH_FREQ)
INS_HNTCH_REF,1
# lowest tracked fundamental 70 Hz (F4-R10, D-173 rpm range, E1 D-173.4: cruise 4 899-5 007 rpm = 1P 81.7-83.4 Hz, hover
#   5 256-5 693 = 87.6-94.9 Hz, all >= 1.1 x 70 = 77 Hz; CL-F4-NOTCH-LOW)
INS_HNTCH_FREQ,70
# bandwidth half the minimum frequency
INS_HNTCH_BW,35
# harmonics 1, 2 (bitmask 3; F4-R8, was 7 = 1-3): 1P and blade pass 2P; one notch set on mean rpm (F405 CPU). D-173: the
#   highest flown rpm is one motor at the 0.81 cap on a fresh pack, 9 663-9 964 rpm (E1 D-173.4): 2P 332 Hz (CL-F4-NOTCH-TOP
#   0.66); 3P would be 498 Hz, 0.4 % under the 500 Hz gyro Nyquist, so 3 harmonics stay off. 3P >= 263 Hz at hover rpm, > 6 x the
#   40 Hz gyro low-pass (EST)
INS_HNTCH_HMNCS,3
# batch-log the first IMU (FFT check of the notch and the 12-15 Hz mode, T-C2-TAP-TEST)
INS_LOG_BAT_MASK,1
# 5 = bit 0 sensor-rate sampling (>= the 1 kHz backend rate, CR-H1-18: GT-18 needs >= 935 Hz) + bit 2 pre- and post-filter
#   gyro (notch check). Read ISBH.SampleRate from the first log; if the F405 drops log blocks (DSF.Dp > 0) set 1
INS_LOG_BAT_OPT,5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 9 Battery (E2: CL-E2-BATT-LOW-MAH, CL-E2-BATT-CRT-MAH; F1/F3 sensor)
# analog voltage + current (FC power board; CoreWing hwdef HAL_BATT_MONITOR_DEFAULT 4)
BATT_MONITOR,4
# voltage divider 11.05 (CoreWing hwdef HAL_BATT_VOLT_SCALE, CR-F3-02); replace with the T-F1-SENSOR-CAL value. FWD_BAT_* reads it
BATT_VOLT_MULT,11.05
# current sensor 64 A/V (CoreWing hwdef HAL_BATT_CURR_SCALE, CR-F3-02, CR-F1-10); replace with the T-F1-SENSOR-CAL value (+/-1.1 %
#   at 70-75 A: the 75 A limiter depends on it)
BATT_AMP_PERVLT,64
# PLACEHOLDER 5 520 mAh = the pack acceptance floor 0.92 x 6 000 (requirements.pack_capacity_min_frac; D-174 Gens Ace 6.0 Ah
#   HV Shorty; R10 5 980 for the 6.5 Ah Ovonic). Before flight set the LOWEST measured T-E2-CAPACITY of the packs flown (D-154).
#   Never the 6 000 nameplate
BATT_CAPACITY,5520
# low at 3 000 mAh remaining (F4-R11, E2 D-173 for the Gens Ace 6.0 Ah HV Shorty, A1 D-174; R10 3 200 for the Ovonic):
#   landing need incl. one 40 s hover go-around + the BATT_CRT reserve; E2: cruise to BATT_LOW 4.66 min (>= 3.5), touchdown
#   1 279 mAh >= 1 200. CL-F4-BATT-LOW reads E2's live claim (E2 to re-run on the Shorty)
BATT_LOW_MAH,3000
# critical at 1 200 mAh = 20 % of 6.0 Ah -> QLAND (F4-R11, E2 D-173 Shorty; was 1 300 for 6.5 Ah)
BATT_CRT_MAH,1200
# voltage backups for LiHV (F4-R11, D-174): 3.60 / 3.50 V per cell resting (BATT_FS_VOLTSRC 1), 0.10 V/cell above the LiPo
#   3.50 / 3.40 of R10 because an LiHV cell rests about 0.1 V higher at the same charge (EST; E2 to confirm from T-E2-CAPACITY's
#   discharge log). The mAh thresholds above are the primary triggers
# low (backup)
BATT_LOW_VOLT,14.4
# critical (backup)
BATT_CRT_VOLT,14.0
# sag-compensated voltage for the failsafe: a transition sag (worst bus 11.87 V at full throttle, CL-E2-V-BUS-WORST) must not trigger it (CR-E2-20)
BATT_FS_VOLTSRC,1
# low action 6 = Loiter to QLand (F4-R8, B3 closure section 2 path 3, H2-4b; was 1 RTL). From a Q mode it goes straight to
#   QLAND (ModeLoiterAltQLand::_enter: previous mode VTOL -> QLAND), never a forward transition. RTL from a Q mode pitches
#   over unless within 1.5 x RTL_RADIUS = 90 m of home AND below Q_RTL_ALT 50 m (mode_rtl.cpp _enter), all tag Plane-4.7.2,
#   read 2026-11-14; SITL S8 2026-11-14. In FW: loiter at the current point down to Q_RTL_ALT 50 m, then QLAND there; the
#   flight card asks the pilot to select RTL (mode slot 6) for the into-wind VTOL approach (C-01)
BATT_FS_LOW_ACT,6
# critical action 4 = QLAND
BATT_FS_CRT_ACT,4
# refuse to arm below 4.25 V/cell (F4-R11, LiHV full 4.35; R10 16.4 = 4.10 for LiPo): the mAh counter assumes a full pack
#   (EST; E2 to confirm the charge level that 4.25 V/cell resting means on the Shorty)
BATT_ARM_VOLT,17.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 10 RC link (ELRS/CRSF, CR-F5-01) and failsafes
# receiver on SERIAL6 (CoreWing DMA UART, F3 CR-F3-02; hwdef DEFAULT_SERIAL6_PROTOCOL RCIN): 23 = RCIN (CRSF)
SERIAL6_PROTOCOL,23
# RSSI from the receiver protocol (CRSF)
RSSI_TYPE,3
# 8480 = bit 8 CRSF passthrough telemetry + bit 13 ELRS 420 kbaud (CR-F5-01: 8448) + bit 5 throttle-at-zero arming check (the firmware default, kept: CR-F4-13)
RC_OPTIONS,8480
# RC failsafe on (default 1, stated); ELRS loss of frames triggers it. The receiver must be set to failsafe mode
#   "No Pulses" (ELRS web UI or Lua; RC-LINK.md, T-F5-BENCH): with "Last Position" or "Set Position" the receiver keeps
#   sending frames and ArduPilot never sees the loss (CDR-26 / CDR-EL-11)
THR_FAILSAFE,1
# RC loss is declared 1.0 s after the last valid frame (default, stated; new line, D-124). 4.7 removed FS_SHORT_TIMEOUT
#   (ReleaseNotes 4.7.0, PR 30350) and added RC_FS_TIMEOUT (PR 31441, range 0.1-10 s): the short failsafe fires at this
#   time. In a Q mode the short event itself selects QLAND (ArduPlane/events.cpp rc_failsafe_short_on_event, tag
#   Plane-4.7.2), so QLAND comes about 1.0-1.2 s after the last frame and does NOT wait for FS_LONG_TIMEOUT.
#   SITL 2026-11-13: QHOVER -> QLAND 1.15 s after the last RC frame (team/F4/sitl/RESULTS.md, S7a)
RC_FS_TIMEOUT,1.0
# short failsafe in FW: 0 = continue in AUTO/GUIDED, else circle; Q modes go to QLAND (Q_OPTIONS bit 5 off)
FS_SHORT_ACTN,0
# long failsafe in FW: 1 = RTL
FS_LONG_ACTN,1
# long failsafe after 5 s (default, stated): fixed-wing modes only (CIRCLE -> RTL). The Q-mode QLAND timer is
#   RC_FS_TIMEOUT above, so the board's "FS_LONG_TIMEOUT 2-3 s" is not needed for QLAND <= 3 s (CDR-26, D-124)
FS_LONG_TIMEOUT,5
# no GCS failsafe: telemetry rides the RC link, so RC failsafe covers it (CR-F5-01)
FS_GCS_ENABL,0
# RTL: 2 = VTOL approach (was 1, C-01, review/NASA-CR-132423-COMPLIANCE.md G-01; CR-132423 p. 35, 38-39, 172): fly home fixed-wing at
#   RTL_ALTITUDE, circle down to Q_RTL_ALT, back-transition INTO THE WIND, then QRTL. Mode 1 back-transitioned on the arrival heading
#   (no downwind limit; vortex-ring risk, CR p. 35). Values on ArduPilot master: 0 off, 1 on, 2 VTOL approach, 3 QRTL always (read 2026-11-13).
#   Keep Q_OPTIONS bit 16 DisableApproach off (262400 does). Name and value 2 read back in SITL 2026-11-13 (S1); a VTOL approach ran once on the stock SITL tailsitter (RESULTS.md). UNVERIFIED on K09-L: S18 (heading)
Q_RTL_MODE,2
# RTL cruise altitude 50 m (>= transition altitude, P:requirements.transition_alt_min_m)
RTL_ALTITUDE,50
# QRTL / VTOL approach altitude 50 m (was 30, C-02, G-01; CR-132423 p. 35, 172): with Q_RTL_MODE 2 the back-transition happens at this
#   height, and transition_alt_min_m is 50 (R-TEST-ORDER). At 50 = RTL_ALTITUDE there is no spiral leg; if H3 lowers the back-transition
#   height the spiral leg returns
Q_RTL_ALT,50
# VTOL-approach spiral radius 60 m (new, C-03, G-01; CR-132423 p. 165 Table 29 bank 9-30 deg, p. 174): = RTL_RADIUS; bank
#   atan(16^2/(9.81 x 60)) = 23.5 deg at 16 m/s, inside 9-30 (EST). Name read back in SITL 2026-11-13 (S1)
Q_FW_LND_APR_RAD,60
# loiter radius at home 60 m (turn radius at 16 m/s, 45 deg bank = 26 m)
RTL_RADIUS,60
WP_LOITER_RAD,60
# approach deceleration 2.0 m/s^2 (default, stated: new line, C-04, G-07; CR-132423 p. 19 Eq. (1): descent angle and deceleration are set together).
#   Sets where the Q_RTL_MODE 2 back-transition starts: 16^2 / (2 x 2.0) = 64 m stop from 16 m/s (EST), inside the 250 m fence.
#   SITL S18 logs the real overshoot past home; lower the value if the tailsitter flare stops short. Range 0.2-5 (master, read 2026-11-13)
Q_TRANS_DECEL,2.0
# EKF failsafe threshold (default 0.8, stated); in Q modes it lands (QLAND), GPS loss lands without position hold
FS_EKF_THRESH,0.8
# flight-mode channel 6 (CR-F5-01: ELRS sends ch 5 as a 2-position bit)
# R-SPIRAL (D-66, A2-R3): every mode below holds the bank with the autopilot's roll loop (spiral t2 3.3-3.5 s is then
#   harmless). Never MANUAL 0, STABILIZE 2, TRAINING 3, ACRO 4 or QACRO 23 here or in INITIAL_MODE (CL-F4-NO-RAW-MODES);
#   no RCn_OPTION selects one (fsw_check.py lint). The GCS can still command any mode: the flight card forbids it
FLTMODE_CH,6
# Slot order (F4-R9, CR-F5-15; was 17 / 18 / 19 / 5 / 7 / 11): the radio puts the Q modes at 988, 1500 and 2012 us and reaches
#   the FW slots only through the latched transition logic (F5 L05 / L06), so a plain switch move cannot pick FBWA from a Q
#   mode (B3 section 2 path 1). S1b pulses 1167 / 1295 / 1423 / 1556 / 1684 / 1817 us -> 17 / 5 / 7 / 18 / 11 / 19
# slot 1: QSTABILIZE (also the transition start mode)
FLTMODE1,17
# slot 2: FBWA (forward transition is started by entering it; only from the timed transition switch)
FLTMODE2,5
# slot 3: CRUISE (heading + altitude hold, airspeed by TECS)
FLTMODE3,7
# slot 4: QHOVER
FLTMODE4,18
# slot 5: RTL
FLTMODE5,11
# slot 6: QLOITER
FLTMODE6,19
# throttle channel range fixed to the radio's CRSF limits (CR-F5-15): F5 picks the transition override value on this range.
#   Do NOT re-calibrate RC3 in Mission Planner; if it is, F5 re-picks the override (team/F5/TRANSITION-SWITCH.md)
RC3_MIN,988
RC3_MAX,2012
# throttle trim at the bottom of the range (F5)
RC3_TRIM,988
# throttle dead zone 30 us (default, stated: CR-F5-15)
RC3_DZ,30
# arm/disarm switch on channel 5 (CR-F5-01, R-ARM-KILL; SA)
RC5_OPTION,153
# channels 6 (the flight-mode channel), 7, 8, 10, 11, 12 carry no aux function (stated, CR-F5-15): no RCn_OPTION selects a
#   flight mode, so FLTMODE_CH is the only way to change mode from the radio
RC6_OPTION,0
RC7_OPTION,0
RC8_OPTION,0
RC10_OPTION,0
RC11_OPTION,0
RC12_OPTION,0
# rudder-stick arming off
ARMING_RUDDER,0
# motor emergency stop on channel 9 (R-ARM-KILL); also the touchdown cut, <= 0.5 s from contact (CR-C5-05b, CL-F4-TD-CUT)
RC9_OPTION,31

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 11 Geofence (RFS)
FENCE_ENABLE,1
# 3 = max altitude + home circle; 7 (adds the polygon) ONLY AFTER the RFS sub-field polygon and the pilot-box exclusion polygon are uploaded and
#   every corner is read back against the field map (plot over satellite imagery, two people, initialled; C-05, G-04; CR-132423 p. 54, 168).
#   Until then FENCE_TYPE stays 3. SITL S9 adds a polygon and an exclusion-zone breach (exclusion support on this board: —, S9)
FENCE_TYPE,3
# breach action 1 = RTL. Plane offers no Q-mode fence action (fence.cpp, tag Plane-4.7.2: RTL / GUIDED / AUTOLAND / report).
#   A breach while hovering (>= 110 m or >= 250 m out, both outside the 90 m / 50 m QRTL cone) therefore starts a forward
#   transition at max(hover, throttle_in): the bounded double-fault case CL-B3-TRANS-PITCH-USE-HOVERTHR 0.848 <= 1.0
#   (F4.md section 4). The breach is at FENCE_ALT_MAX itself; FENCE_MARGIN is a notice only (H2, AC_Fence.cpp 4.7)
FENCE_ACTION,1
# 110 m AGL against 400 ft = 121.9 m (P:mission.ceiling_ft_agl)
FENCE_ALT_MAX,110
# 250 m circle around home, inside VLOS 500 m (P:requirements.vlos_max_m)
FENCE_RADIUS,250
FENCE_MARGIN,10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 12 Board and sensor placement (F3, CR-F3-02; CoreWing F405 Wing V2, D-173b)
# FC flat, arrow toward the nose (-x): fixed-wing attitude (the tailsitter code rotates for hover)
AHRS_ORIENTATION,0
# GPS on SERIAL5: 5 = GPS
SERIAL5_PROTOCOL,5
# IMU position from the CG in the FRD body frame (m): F3's IMU (-0.010, 0.046, 0.039) aircraft frame (CR-F3-20: board
#   4 mm higher) from the D-62 CG x 0.0490 (P:cg.x_target_m), z +0.0185 (P:cg.z_target_m; A3's CL-A3-CG-Z 0.0186).
#   CALC-F4-SENSOR-POS. F3 re-runs CALC-F3-OFFSETS on the R6 bay (CR-F4-19); re-measure as built
INS_POS1_X,0.059
INS_POS1_Y,0.046
INS_POS1_Z,-0.0205
# second IMU slot, same chip position (F3; the CoreWing has two IMUs)
INS_POS2_X,0.059
INS_POS2_Y,0.046
INS_POS2_Z,-0.0205
# GPS antenna position from the CG (m): F3's GPS centre (0.075, 0, 0.178) (CR-F3-20) from the same D-62 CG (4.6+ name). CALC-F4-SENSOR-POS
GPS1_POS_X,-0.026
GPS1_POS_Y,0
GPS1_POS_Z,-0.1595
# compass orientation auto-detected and stored (F3 expects 36 on the 45-deg mast pad)
COMPASS_AUTO_ROT,2
